{"author":{"id":"1832e4168d45d4ef31531146dbc743bb950a5dd543b15fd8e3a076fd976bfdef"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790972086,"nonce":"4DV5X+eOQe8cGnKLdp68mxRtq70=","title":"generated HashLink code defines HlBytes, which a shared runtime crate cannot name","message":"Since c980074d4d6e099e136fcc82e634a4afe09bda2e76120d68f850ee909f02189e, the HashLink output has defined `pub struct HlBytes` (haxe.io.Bytes' layout) in each adapter's generated model, and passes `*mut HlBytes` to `Buffer::from_hl`. A runtime module that is its own crate, as hlwgpu's hl_xidl now is for both hlwgpu and hlwindow, cannot name a type its adapter generates. Its `Buffer::from_hl` takes its own `HlBytes`, and the generated `*mut crate::HlBytes` does not match it.\n\nThe runtime should own the layout. Generated code names `runtime::HlBytes` in Buffer and BufferMut arguments and in `__hl_buffer_result_copy`, and no longer defines it. The adapter's `crate::runtime` then provides `HlBytes` beside `Buffer`.","files":null}]}